>
>
>What is the purpose of praying. On occasion, I have prayed accidently
>and the message is "<god> is pleased. Your <stuff> glows blue for a
>moment." <-- What does this do?

Praying is a very usefull, often ass-saving, occupation that tries to do
every once in a while...
Many nifty things can happen when you pray...
  - The amber glow ( the <stuff> that glowed has just been blessed (nice) or
	uncursed (wonderful)) The blue glow is the same thing ( but I think
	an older version of the game...

  - If you pray when you're weak with hunger you almost always have your tummy
    filled ( really saves on food )

  - If a golden glow surrounds you, you are healed to full hit-points+

  - Any abilities that have been dropped down (ie: due to poisons et all) can
	be restored

   note : if you have the older version with the blue glow, having the golden
	  glow surround you does all three of the previous items at one time.

  - You can have your luck increase

  - Hallucination, blindness, confusion, et al can be removed

  - chains can be removed from balls

  - The gods could give you magic items of varying powers and types.

  - Luck may be gained

  - Lycanthropy removed

  - it goes on and on and on and on.......

  Of course all of these things only happen if your god is happy with you
  ( ie: from #offering juicy monsters as sacrifices, or being properly
        dutiful to your alignment )

